2101 O’Neil Avenue
Cheyenne, WY 82001
RE: Request for Increase in Contract Prices Due to Force Majeure Event
Dear Mr. LaVoy,
Welborn Sullivan Meek & Tooley, P.C. represents Dan Hart Patrol Service, LLC (“DIIP”).
This letter is a request to amend the Happy Jack Landfill Phase 2, Cells 1 and 2 Construction and
Cell 3 Excavation “Contract” by and among the “City” of Cheyenne, DHP et. al. Specifically it
is a request to increase the per unit prices to be paid by the City to DHP as described in the enclosed
Request for Information.
DHP is requesting the per unit prices be increased due the unforeseen, uncontrollable and
non-seasonal spike in the price of diesel fuel. DHP is likely to incur a substantial loss if the per
unit prices are not adjusted to account for the extraordinary increase in fuel cost. Under Section
41 of the Contract, the increase in the diesel fuel cost is a force majeure event because it is “an
occurrence beyond the control of the parties”
... which “dissuade[s]
... the performance required
by” DHP due to the near certainty that DHP will lose money.
Accordingly, DHP respectfully
requests that the per unit prices be increased as described in the enclosed document. If you have
any questions, please feel free to contact me or Steven Gerber (307-756-2835).
Sincerely,
Enclosure
```

